></g></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Ce<sup>3+</sup>   E° = +1.74 V<br><br>\nPositive SRP and higher SRP means greater\noxidising power. So, Ce<sup>4+</sup> wants to reduce to Ce<sup>3+</sup>.\nIndicates Ce<sup>4+</sup> is less stable than Ce<sup>3+</sup>."},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं :<br><br>कथन I : Ce<sup>4+</sup> / Ce<sup>3+</sup> के लिए E<sup>o</sup> मूल्य + 1.74 V है।<br><br>कथन II : Ce Ce<sup>4+</sup> स्थिति में Ce<sup>3+</sup> स्थिति की तुलना में अधिक स्थिर है।<br><br>उपरोक्त कथनों के आधार पर, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सबसे उपयुक्त उत्तर चुनें :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"कथन I गलत है लेकिन कथन II सही है"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों गलत हैं"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कथन I सही है लेकिन कथन II गलत है"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"inner-transition-elements-lanthanoids-and-actinoids","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-16th-march-morning-shift","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-16th-march-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"fY08CRP8mlUgZk3BNo1kmht5wqw","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 16th March Morning Shift","permalink":"in-chromotography-technique-the-purification-of-compound-is-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-byailvkcwpsf6xc9","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"In chromotography technique, the purification of compound is independent of :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Solubility of the compound"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Mobility or flow of solvent system"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Physical state of the pure compound"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Length of the column or TLC plate"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>The purification of a compound using chromatography is dependent on several factors, including the solubility of the compound, the mobility or flow of the solvent system, and the length of the column or TLC plate. However, it is not typically dependent on the physical state of the pure compound. Here&#39;s why :</p>\n<p>Option A : The solubility of the compound in the mobile phase and its interaction with the stationary phase are key factors in determining how the compound will migrate in a chromatographic system. Hence, the solubility of the compound does affect its purification.</p>\n<p>Option B : The mobility or flow of the solvent system, often referred to as the mobile phase in chromatography, also plays a significant role in the separation of components in the mixture. The rate at which the mobile phase moves can influence how far and how quickly the components of the mixture will travel.</p>\n<p>Option C : The physical state (solid, liquid, gas) of the pure compound is usually not a factor in the purification process in chromatography. Whether a compound is solid, liquid, or gas does not typically affect its ability to be separated by chromatography, as it is the interactions between the compound and the stationary/mobile phases that are key.</p>\n<p>Option D : The length of the column or TLC plate can impact the degree of separation achieved in chromatography. A longer column or TLC plate can provide more opportunities for the interactions that drive the separation process, often leading to better separation of the components.</p>\n<p>So, Option C is correct : The physical state of the pure compound is usually not a factor in its purification by chromatography.</p>"},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"क्रोमैटोग्राफी तकनीक में, यौगिक की शुद्धता निम्न में से किस पर निर्भर नहीं करती है :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"यौगिक की घुलनशीलता"},{"identifier":"B","content":"सॉल्वेंट सिस्टम की गतिशीलता या प्रवाह"},{"identifier":"C","content":"शुद्ध यौगिक की भौतिक अवस्था"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कॉलम या TLC प्लेट की लंबाई"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"purification-of-organic-compounds","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-16th-march-morning-shift","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-16th-march-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"7WCoZ43jUqQDISg2wd1kmht9z0m","chapter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 16th March Morning Shift","permalink":"a-group-of-15-element-which-is-a-metal-and-forms-a-hydride-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-9fwn32ix5ec6ej94","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"A group of 15 element, which is a metal and forms a hydride with strongest reducing power among group 15 hydrides. The element is :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"As"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Sb"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Bi"},{"identifier":"D","content":"P"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"BiH<sub>3</sub> is the strongest reducing agent among the hydrides of 15 group elements as Bi – H bond dissociation energy is very less."},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"वह समूह का 15 तत्व, जो एक धातु है और समूह 15 हाइड्राइड्स में सबसे शक्तिशाली घटक हाइड्राइड बनाता है। वह तत्व है :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"As"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Sb"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Bi"},{"identifier":"D","content":"P"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry",